                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "48f5e9ee-4d84-3269-8e38-76f421e34993",
                        "entry_id": "f1289151-c26d-3663-9900-2b3bb798e2ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of wood anemone (Anemone nemorosa)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "681929c3-5a31-45ef-8f70-1d7e533944c5",
                                "sense_id": "48f5e9ee-4d84-3269-8e38-76f421e34993",
                                "text": "Herba venti, Anemone. Wind flower, the juyce snuffed up the nose purgeth the head, it cleanseth filthy ulcers, encreaseth milk in nurses, and outwardly by ointment helps Leprosyes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d286f26-af84-4634-a806-6a108a20b153",
                                "sense_id": "48f5e9ee-4d84-3269-8e38-76f421e34993",
                                "text": "“When windflowers blossom on the sea\nAnd fishes skim along the plain,\nThen we who part this weary day,\nThen you and I shall meet again.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "978bc0c8-798f-4a8b-9835-d163c93d8d8a",
                                "sense_id": "48f5e9ee-4d84-3269-8e38-76f421e34993",
                                "text": "The first windflowers were out, and all the wood seemed pale with the pallor of endless little anemones, sprinkling the shaken floor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f3889510-1aac-4b15-bf0d-e70a7fe9c355",
                                "sense_id": "48f5e9ee-4d84-3269-8e38-76f421e34993",
                                "text": "“[…] We spent an hour in a hazel copse, picking primroses and looking at the little white windflowers. One doesn’t pick the windflowers,” he explained, “because in an hour they’re withered. […]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30d037d5-4fa2-4386-b5b9-aff804cc2dff",
                                "sense_id": "48f5e9ee-4d84-3269-8e38-76f421e34993",
                                "text": "Here is spring were celandine, marsh marigold, wind-flower, primrose, cowslip and dog's violet."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
